# banned-terms.txt.example
#
# Copy this file to tools/banned-terms.txt and replace the lines below with
# real words that must never appear in the repo. .gitignore keeps
# tools/banned-terms.txt out of git, so the real words stay on your machine.
#
# One term per line. Matching ignores case and treats each line as plain
# text (no wildcards). Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# What to list:
#   - employer name and its short forms
#   - real host names and cluster names
#   - database names, service names, schema names
#   - GoldenGate extract and replicat names
#   - names of colleagues and teams
#   - internal domain names
CHANGE_ME_EMPLOYER_NAME
CHANGE_ME_DB_NAME
CHANGE_ME_SCHEMA_NAME
